1.050.157  (57) Abstract: Some methods of analyzing one or more sections of a central nervous system of a patient comprise, for each of thesection(s), from data the includes one or more 3D representations of the section, segmenting each of the 3D representation(s) into ventral   and dorsal portions and, for at least one of the 3D representation(s), determining a mean curvature of at least a region of a surface of   the dorsal portion and/or a mean curvature of at least a region of a surface of the ventral portion. Each of the section(s) can include at least a portion of a brainstem of the patient.

